
/*
  ================================================================
                 JARVIS V4 - COMPACT CORRECTED FIRMWARE
  ================================================================

  BOARD       : ESP32
  mDNS        : jarvis-v4.local
  Dashboard   : HTTP 80
  WiFi Portal : JARVIS-V4-SETUP / 192.168.4.1
  MQTT        : homeassistant.local:1883

  WIFI:
  - Dedicated wildcard DNS and captive portal HTTP server.
  - WiFiManager never competes for HTTP port 80.
  - WPA2/WPA3 router compatibility; no restrictive security floor.
  - WiFi modem power save disabled (WIFI_PS_NONE) for handshake stability.
  - Submitted credentials retained in RAM until WiFi connection succeeds.
  - WiFi and MQTT settings saved and verified in NVS after connection.
  - Saved credentials loaded explicitly on boot and reconnect.
  - Disconnect reason codes reported on Serial.

  HARDWARE:
  - GPIO2 WiFi status LED: ON=connected, blink=portal, OFF=offline.
  - Main gate locks only after confirmed Close Limit.
  - Close timeout stops motor and never activates the lock.
  - Local inputs and gate state machine run before networking.
  - BOOT held for five seconds triggers factory reset.
  ================================================================
*/

